  "title": "Software Defensibility in the era of AI coding",
  "description": "If the cost of building software is approaching 0, is the value of building software is also approaching 0? If most software can be easily replicated by AI, how can we defend our products after we've built it? This talk discusses what have traditionally been considered moats for software products, why they aren't really moats, and why we should, as builders, continue building.\n\nSeating for this session is first-come, first-served. Add it to your schedule to plan your day and arrive early to secure a spot.",
